            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Disclosed herein are embodiments of a spinal implant having structures that incorporate a solid material and a porous material. The solid material provides the implant with an outer shell for structural integrity while the porous material, distributed within an interior of the implant as a lattice structure for example, promotes visibility of the implant in radiological imaging, promotes bony ingrowth and cell attachment and improves wicking.</p>
            </abstract>
